  </catalogueLinks>
  <sharedProfiles>
    <profile name="Pikemen" typeId="a5d3-6ea8-6425-5123" typeName="Ability" hidden="false" id="5f90-b8cc-37c8-7c2a">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="bc69-55f2-6b4e-18e7">Pikemen can not enter dense terrain (even partially). They still may be in a defended position on higher ground or behind a low obstacle as usual, but can only claim defended status when fighting to the front.




An enemy does not receive charge bonuses when charging Pikemen in the front, nor do Pikemen receive any charge bonus themselves.






A Pikemen stand cannot support or be supported by other infantry - only by other Pikemen stands. In all other respects they count as infantry (movement/pursuit etc.).</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
  </sharedProfiles>
</catalogue>
